{"assumptions":["Run sequence: the spec was still over the feature size budget, so the work is split into three runs. Run 1 (this spec) covers the read side of the API: overdue rule, overdue list, customer and bucket filters, and authentication (REQ-1, REQ-2, REQ-3, REQ-4, REQ-14, REQ-19). Run 2 covers sending, reminder history, failures, invoice detail and unknown-invoice handling (old REQ-7 to REQ-13, REQ-18, plus the latest reminder outcome on list items, old AC-2.3). Run 3 covers the React screens. Run 2 and Run 3 requirements are kept under suggestions.","REQ-2 no longer returns 'latest reminder outcome' in this run, because the reminder history table it reads from is built in Run 2. Run 2 adds the field back (old AC-2.3).","No client repository or schema was available (current-behaviour has no claims), so the spec makes no claim about the client's real status values, due-date column type or token claims. These are settings: the open-status list and the staff claim rule (claim type + value) have no built-in client values and are set at deployment once confirmed against the client's system. Tests set them explicitly (e.g. ['open'], 'user_type' = 'staff') as test values only.","Invoice data from the existing database is read through one invoice source adapter that returns logical fields (invoice ID, invoice number, customer ID and name, amount, raw status value, due date as a calendar date or null). OverduePolicy works only on these logical fields. Mapping the client's real columns to them, including turning a timestamp due date into a calendar date in the business time zone if the column is not date-typed, must be confirmed before build and is not a tested behaviour of this run.","Staff vs non-staff: a staff user is a principal whose existing-API token holds the configured staff claim. Any other principal with a valid token (service or integration clients, non-staff user accounts) is non-staff and gets 403. No token, an expired token or an invalid token gets 401.","The bucket conflict is settled in favour of fixed buckets (old REQ-5, 2 of 3 drafts, matches ASM-4's literal 7–30 / 31–60 / 60+). The rule is part of REQ-4 (AC-4.4). Old REQ-6 (lowest bucket starts at the threshold) is dropped. If the threshold is set below 7, invoices overdue by fewer than 7 days appear only in the unfiltered list.","An invoice can be overdue only if its status value is in the configured open-status list. Any other status (paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed, credited, or unknown) and any null due date is never overdue. If the list is empty, no invoice is overdue. Q-4 still holds: paid and cancelled invoices drop off automatically.","Invoices, customers and paid/cancelled status are read from the client's existing .NET 8 API / Postgres database (ASM-1). This run adds no new table.","The overdue threshold is configurable with a default of 7. An invoice is overdue when today's local date in the configured business time zone (Europe/London in the examples) minus the due date is at least the threshold. 'Days overdue' means calendar days since the due date (ASM-2, ASM-3, ASM-10, ASM-11).","ASM-4's '60+' bucket is read as 61+ so it does not overlap 31–60. Bucket limits are inclusive.","Today's date comes from an injectable clock so tests can fix it. Day counting lives in one policy class (OverduePolicy) that takes the clock, threshold, open-status list and time zone.","Status codes in this run: 401 unauthenticated, 403 authenticated principal without the configured staff claim, 400 invalid bucket.","Proposed API path for this run: GET /api/invoices/overdue?customerId=&daysOverdue={bucket}.","NFR-1 uses the largest data volume any draft gave."],"critic":[{"finding":"The open-status list has no built-in value and an empty list silently means 'no invoice is ever overdue', but nothing covers a missing or empty setting at deployment (no startup failure, no error), so a misconfiguration gives an empty overdue list that looks correct.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"The staff claim type and value have no built-in value, but nothing says what happens when they are not configured (startup failure, every request 403, or every request allowed), and no AC covers it.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Q-1 says 'any authenticated staff user, using the existing API's authentication', but REQ-19 assumes the existing API's tokens carry a claim that tells staff from non-staff, and current-behaviour has no claims to back that up, so this new 403 gate may block every real user.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-1.1 to AC-1.5 and AC-1.7 are checked only through the internal OverduePolicy.Evaluate method (unit level), not through GET /api/invoices/overdue, so the overdue rule, the time-zone boundary and the status filter are never shown at the public API.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Only a known customer with no invoices is covered (AC-3.1 returns an empty 200); nothing says what happens with a customerId that does not exist or is badly formed (e.g. not a valid ID type), unlike the 400 that REQ-4 defines for a bad bucket.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No failure path is defined for when the client's existing database or invoice source adapter cannot be reached or returns bad rows (e.g. an invoice with a missing customer), and there is no AC for a 200 with an empty list when nothing is overdue at all.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'Return every invoice currently classified as overdue' has no ordering or pagination, even though NFR-1 expects 5,000+ open invoices, so the size and order of the response cannot be tested.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The actual query-string values for the buckets are never given: the ACs use en-dash labels ('7–30', '61+') while AC-4.3's invalid example uses a hyphen ('5-6'), so the accepted daysOverdue token format is unclear at the API.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The assumptions say an invalid token (bad signature, wrong issuer) gets 401, but AC-14.1 only tests no token and an expired token.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"daysOverdue for an invoice not yet due (due date after today) is not defined (negative, zero or left out), even though Evaluate returns daysOverdue for invoices that are not overdue (AC-1.1 returns 6).","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The text says both billing emails and invoice amounts stay out of logs, but the metric only counts billing emails, which this run never reads (sending is in Run 2), so the check passes by default; amounts and customer names, which this run does return, are not checked.","reqId":"NFR-3","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The 10,000-invoice / 5,000-open volume is justified only as 'the largest data volume any draft gave', with no link to an answer, assumption or the client's real data.","reqId":"NFR-1","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-2.2's 'no overdue flag was written to the invoice record' and AC-1.6's 'invoice record unchanged' need a direct check of the client's database, which is not a public surface of this API.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Overdue is computed on every request by reading the client's live production Postgres directly through an adapter, but nothing limits query load or the access level (read-only role) on the client's existing database.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":7,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The accepted assumptions ASM-5 (later bounces count as failures) and ASM-13 (only immediate send errors count) contradict each other, and the spec silently picks ASM-13 in outOfScope without saying the conflict was settled.","rubric":1,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L9 size","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 ≤ 1,000 ms at the API with 10,000 invoices (at least 5,000 of them open), with or without filters","text":"The overdue list endpoint meets the stated latency at the stated data volumes, with or without filters."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 customer billing email addresses found in application log output across the whole automated acceptance test run","text":"Customer PII (billing email addresses) and invoice amounts are kept out of application logs."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"100% of new Invoice Reminders endpoints return 401 without a valid token and 403 with a valid token lacking the configured staff claim (checked by an automated endpoint sweep)","text":"All Invoice Reminders endpoints require staff authentication."}],"outOfScope":["Run 2 of the sequence (not this run): sending a reminder email for an overdue invoice (I-2), recording append-only reminder history with sender and time (I-3, Q-3, Q-7, Q-8), recording and showing send failures (I-4, ASM-13), the invoice detail API with history (I-7), rejecting sends for non-overdue, missing-billing-email and unknown invoices, and adding the latest reminder outcome to the overdue list items; see suggestions for the moved requirements REQ-7 to REQ-13 and REQ-18","Run 3 of the sequence (not this run): building the React overdue list screen (table, customer and bucket filters, per-row 'Send reminder' button, link to detail) and invoice detail screen (amount, due date, history, failures, 'Send reminder' button while overdue) described in I-6 and I-7; this run delivers only the overdue list API those screens use","Run 3 of the sequence (not this run): disabling the 'Send reminder' button while a send is in progress (Q-5, ASM-14) and showing the send result on screen","Payments and recording payments (paid/cancelled status is only read from the existing system)","Customer logins or any customer-facing screens","SMS reminders","Detecting delivery failures after hand-off (bounces, complaint/provider webhooks, later rejections); only immediate email-sender errors count as failures (ASM-13)","Automatic or scheduled reminders; every send is started by staff","A stored 'overdue' status on the invoice or a daily job to set it; overdue is computed at query time (Q-6)","Server-side duplicate-send protection (cooldown, daily limit, duplicate check) (Q-5)","Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user' (Q-1)","Creating or editing invoices, customers or billing emails (ASM-1)","Sending to more than one contact per customer (Q-2)","Editing or deleting reminder history entries (Q-3)","Configurable email templates or wording (ASM-9, ASM-15)","Days-overdue buckets that move with the configured threshold; buckets are fixed at 7–30, 31–60, 61+","Changing the existing API's token issuance or claim contents; this run only reads the configured staff claim"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"open-status list configured as ['open'], threshold the default 7, business time zone Europe/London, the injected clock set to 2026-10-15, and invoices with status 'open' due 2026-10-08 and 2026-10-09","id":"AC-1.1","level":"unit","then":"the call for the invoice due 2026-10-08 returns overdue = true and daysOverdue = 7, and the call for the invoice due 2026-10-09 returns overdue = false and daysOverdue = 6","when":"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice"},{"given":"open-status list configured as ['open'], threshold set to 10, today 2026-10-15, and invoices with status 'open' due 2026-10-07, 2026-10-06 and 2026-10-05","id":"AC-1.2","level":"unit","then":"the calls return overdue = false for the invoices due 2026-10-07 and 2026-10-06, and overdue = true for the invoice due 2026-10-05","when":"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice"},{"given":"threshold 7, open-status list configured as ['open'], and seven invoices each 20 days past due with statuses paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed and credited","id":"AC-1.3","level":"unit","then":"every call returns overdue = false","when":"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice"},{"given":"threshold 7, open-status list configured as ['open'], and an invoice with status 'open' and a null due date","id":"AC-1.4","level":"unit","then":"the call returns overdue = false and throws no exception","when":"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for it"},{"given":"open-status list configured as ['open'], business time zone Europe/London, default threshold, and an invoice with status 'open' due 2026-09-01","id":"AC-1.5","level":"unit","then":"the first call returns daysOverdue = 6 and overdue = false, and the second returns daysOverdue = 7 and overdue = true","when":"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called at instant 2026-09-07T22:30Z (23:30 on 7 Sep local), then at 2026-09-07T23:30Z (00:30 on 8 Sep local)"},{"given":"open-status list configured as ['open'], an invoice with status 'open' due 6 days ago is not in the overdue list response, and no job or data change runs","id":"AC-1.6","level":"api","then":"the response now holds the invoice with daysOverdue = 7, and the invoice record in the existing database is unchanged","when":"the injected clock moves forward 1 day and the overdue list is requested again"},{"given":"open-status list configured as ['unpaid','part-paid'] and threshold 7, with invoices 10 days past due whose status values are 'unpaid', 'part-paid' and 'open'","id":"AC-1.7","level":"unit","then":"the calls return overdue = true for 'unpaid' and 'part-paid' and overdue = false for 'open'","when":"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice"}],"ears":"The invoice reminders system shall classify an invoice as overdue, working this out on every request and never storing it, only when the invoice's status value is in the configured open-status list (which has no built-in client value and is set at deployment), its due date is not null, and the number of calendar days from its due date to today's date, both taken in the configured business time zone, is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7).","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-10","ASM-11"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"open-status list configured as ['open'], today 2026-10-15, threshold 7, and in the existing database: open invoice A for customer 'Crumb & Co' with amount 125.50 due 2026-10-01, open invoice B due 2026-10-12, invoice C due 2026-09-01 with status paid, and invoice D due 2026-09-01 with status cancelled","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"the response is 200 and holds only invoice A, with its invoice number, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 125.50, due date 2026-10-01 and daysOverdue 14","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list"},{"given":"invoice A is in the overdue list","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"invoice A is no longer in the response and no overdue flag was written to the invoice record","when":"its status in the existing system is changed to paid and the overdue list is requested again"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the Invoice Reminders API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue, each with invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue (calendar days since the due date).","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-6","Q-4","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"customer X has 2 overdue invoices, customer Y has 1 overdue invoice, and customer Z has none","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"the first response holds exactly customer X's 2 invoices and the second response is 200 with an empty list","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with customerId = X, then with customerId = Z"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only the overdue invoices that belong to that customer.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"default threshold 7 and overdue invoices at 7, 30, 31, 60, 61 and 90 days overdue","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"the responses hold {7, 30}, {31, 60} and {61, 90}","when":"the overdue list is requested with bucket 7–30, then 31–60, then 61+"},{"given":"customers X and Y each have overdue invoices at 10 and 45 days","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"the first response holds only X's 45-day invoice and the second holds only X's 10-day invoice","when":"the overdue list is requested with customerId = X and bucket 31–60, then with customerId = X and bucket 7–30"},{"given":"any overdue invoices","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"the response is 400 with a validation error naming the bucket parameter","when":"the overdue list is requested with an unknown bucket value such as '5-6'"},{"given":"the overdue threshold is set to 5 and an open invoice is 6 days past due","id":"AC-4.4","level":"api","then":"the invoice is in the unfiltered response and is in none of the three bucket responses","when":"the overdue list is requested without a bucket, then with bucket 7–30, 31–60 and 61+"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall inside the named fixed bucket (7–30, 31–60 or 61+, limits inclusive, not shifted by the configured overdue threshold), or respond 400 with a validation error when the bucket value is not one of these.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-3","ASM-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"no token, and separately an expired token","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"each response is 401 with no invoice or customer data in the body","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called, with and without customer and bucket filters"},{"given":"the staff claim rule configured as claim type 'user_type' with value 'staff', and a valid token carrying that claim and no other role","id":"AC-14.2","level":"api","then":"the response is 200, not 401 or 403","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called"}],"ears":"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint has no valid authentication token from the existing API, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email or changing data.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"the staff claim rule configured as claim type 'user_type' with value 'staff', and a valid, unexpired token whose 'user_type' claim is 'service', and separately one with no 'user_type' claim","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"each response is 403 and its body holds no invoice or customer data","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called with each token, with and without customer and bucket filters"},{"given":"the staff claim rule reconfigured as claim type 'role' with value 'bakery-staff', and a valid token carrying 'user_type' = 'staff' but no 'role' = 'bakery-staff' claim","id":"AC-19.2","level":"api","then":"the response is 403, and a token carrying 'role' = 'bakery-staff' gets 200","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called"}],"ears":"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint carries a valid, unexpired token from the existing API that does not hold the configured staff claim (claim type and value set in configuration, with no built-in client value), then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 403 without returning invoice or customer data or changing data.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1","ASM-1"],"stability":0.3333333333333333}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":["The overdue list endpoint shall meet stated latency requirements at stated data volumes, with or without filters applied.","Customer PII, specifically billing email addresses, and invoice amounts shall be kept out of application logs."]}}